<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gudfred</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 810</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Godfred, Godfrid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gudfred was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> in the early 9th century and an opponent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>. In 808 he attacked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obotrites">Obotrites</a>, allies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a>, destroyed their trading port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reric">Reric</a> and moved its merchants to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hedeby">Hedeby</a>, and he strengthened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danevirke">Danevirke</a> earthwork across southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jutland">Jutland</a>. He was murdered in 810 after raiding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frisia">Frisia</a>, as Charlemagne prepared for war against him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gudfred.jpg" alt="Gudfred" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Erico Olai Tormio (publisher) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kong_G%C3%B8trik_den_Gavmilde.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
